    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. the infrasound thing definitely explains the chest feeling. but when i listen really closely, it doesn't just feel like random wind or pressure... it feels like it's pulsed. almost like it's modulated. if someone were actually trying to transmit data using those low frequencies during a pressure shift like that, what kind of tech would they even use to make it bypass standard radio detection?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
